    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106-a7">

                <pb facs="0255" n="199" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg199"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Liverpool</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-04-07"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 7,
                        1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: I am in receipt of your note,
                    inclosing a copy of fog-signals proposed by the board of trade, and herewith beg
                    to hand you my report on the same.</p>
                <p>The signals A, B, C are very good, with the exception of the interval given,
                    which, in my opinion, should not be longer than two minutes at the most.</p>
                <p>The four following signals would, I think, be of great use in channels or rivers,
                    as giving a system to the signals, with the exception of the last, which I think
                    would be apt to lead to error, or be confusing. I do not think these signals
                    would be of much service on the high seas.</p>
                <p>If I might be allowed to suggest, I think it ought to be compulsory to have more
                    uniformity in the size of bell, horn, and whistle for fog purposes, as these
                    instruments may often be seen totally unfit for these purposes.</p>
                <p>Yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>S. METCALFE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Commander Steamship
                            Belgic</hi>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ismay, Imrie</hi> &amp; Co.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
